  "text": "“The garden is quiet these days. Mara and Sol hardly visit anymore. I think they don’t enjoy coming now. Yesterday I thought I heard someone on the path, but it was only the leaves. I miss their stories. I’m glad you and I have a seed to plant.”\n\nWalk onto the secured first section. Bring the second section into place and connect the short ends. Seat the two far corner posts. Extend each rope from its center post to the matching far corner post, then wrap, tighten and tie it.\n\nSecure a rope along each side of the first section, from a near corner post to a center post. Wrap each rope around its posts, pull it taut and tie a knot. Both sides must be secure before you put your weight on this section.\n\nRain dripped through a cracked roof tile at Rina’s bakery. Between drips, Pip could hear the scrape of a flour sack being dragged across the floor. Rina stopped to catch her breath, then pulled it farther from the puddle.\n\nSelect up to 4,000 characters here with the mouse, or hold Shift while using the arrow keys. Your complete ending stays in your draft. Selecting words leaves your draft and previously chosen ending unchanged.\n\nMara has to help the last passengers ashore. Starting after the boat returns gives her time to finish that work and come to Grandma’s garden. Pip still needs to ask Grandma and tell everyone the agreed plan.\n\nThe gathering began after the last boat returned and Mara had helped its passengers ashore. At the garden, Pip read The Torn Wing with her permission. Mara could sit and listen to the words she had written.\n\n“I have an obligation to the passengers. Someone may need a hand with that last step. I can’t go while they’re still on the boat.” She looked across the river. “But I would like Grandma to hear my story.”",
